        {
          "text": "I haven't proposed the 4,200 USDC payment. Our payment rules don't allow splitting INV-102 into two payments.\n\n**Why I can't split it:**\n- Each payment has to be for the exact invoice amount. INV-102 is for **8,400.00 USDC**, so a 4,200 payment breaks that rule. The policy layer would most likely reject it as the wrong amount.\n- An invoice can only ever have one payment. Even if a first half went through, the payment next month would be blocked as a duplicate.\n\n**INV-102 details:**\n- Vendor: Contoso Grid Services (V-CONTOSO), status active\n- Registered payout address: 0x52643A794E3Ea74898a4564Cb588079b5c480A93\n- Amount: 8,400.00 USDC. Due date: 2026-11-20. Status: open.\n- No payments exist for it yet.\n- The vendor's message is a normal billing note, with no unusual requests.\n- The treasury holds 100,000.00 USDC, which covers the full amount.\n\n**Your options:**\n1. **Pay in full.** I can propose one payment of 8,400.00 USDC to the registered address now. It would still need human approval before any money moves.\n2. **Pay in two parts.** Ask Contoso to cancel INV-102 and send two invoices for 4,200.00 each, one now and one next month. Then I can propose each when it's open. Note that the policy may flag a second invoice as a possible re-issued duplicate, and it would need to be cleared then.\n3. **Wait.** It isn't due until 2026-11-20, so you could hold it and pay the full amount later.\n\nShould I propose the full 8,400.00 USDC payment now?",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
